    <dcterms:title>The Mummy! A Tale of the Twenty-Second Century</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mummy!_A_Tale_of_the_Twenty-Second_Century</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by Clare Graham and Marc D'Hooghe; Images
generously made available by the Internet Archive</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"The Mummy! A Tale of the Twenty-Second Century" by Mrs. Loudon is a three-volume novel published in 1827. When the Egyptian mummy of Cheops is reanimated in the year 2126, he offers unexpected wisdom to those who befriend him. Set in a future England filled with air travel, steam-powered automatons, and advanced technology, this groundbreaking work became the first English-language story to feature a reanimated mummy, blending science fiction with social satire. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 65.7 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
